WEBVTT

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.250
Every Pokémon will belong
to Team Rocket.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.540
Ahh...

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.620
What great weather!

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.140
Everyone ready for another day of
exciting contest rehearsals?

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.060
Huh?

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.170
Where’s Pochama?

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.780
Come on, Pochama,
why are you sleeping?!

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.170
Tomorrow’s the big event.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.740
You need to focus!

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.140
Come on, Pochama!

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.280
Pochama!

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.650
You should be their role model,

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.610
but you just keep slacking off.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:42.170
These days, you keep waking up late
and dozing off after eating...

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.210
Hold it!

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:49.590
Pochama!

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.670
Pochama!

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.700
Excuse me!
That Pochama is my...

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.270
Huh?

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.100
Pochama?

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.520
Oh, no!

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.000
Yeah... Yeah...

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.360
Got it. We’ll be right there!

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.000
What happened?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.360
Hikari’s Pochama was kidnapped!

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.130
Kidnapped?!

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.830
Hikari was in Sinnoh, correct?

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.010
Yeah!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.300
There’s something
I was meaning to report to you.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:48.050
There’s been an influx of
Pokémon disappearaces in Sinnoh lately.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.650
Huh?! That many?!

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.280
And they’re all
completely unexplained.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.680
No time to waste!
We’re going!

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.870
I’m going too, Father!

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.160
Okay. But look after yourself.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.630
Yeah!

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:06.290
Now that’s settled!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.880
Off to Sinnoh, we...

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.790
<i>Go!</i>

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.150
Hikari!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.040
Satoshi...
Koharu and Go, too...

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.660
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.860
It’s fine.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.250
At least, that’s what I’d like to say...

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.850
But it’s not fine, is it...?

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.880
Your beloved partner
was stolen from you...

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.260
I thought you might need something,
so I bought these!

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:22.200
Nice and hot croquettes!
Can’t work on an empty stomach, right?

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.470
Satoshi...

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:31.070
This isn’t like me...
I’m sorry.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.150
This time, I really will be fine!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.570
Huh? A lookalike?!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:42.450
Yeah. She even had
the same clothes and hat.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.340
Isn’t that...?

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.360
Yeah.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.240
Just recently, we met someone
who looked just like Koharu, too.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.620
There is that saying,
everyone has three identical lookalikes...

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.110
I feel like this was different.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:02.720
She went into this strange, shining hole
while carrying Pochama...

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.260
A strange, shining hole?

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.720
Yeah.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:08.390
And she vanished along with it.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.830
Something like an Ultra Hole?

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.340
I don’t know...

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.540
Then, when I went to see Ms. Junsa...

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:20.070
Actually, there have been
several other cases just like yours.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:27.270
Based on the witness reports so far,
the holes appear to be connected to some other place,

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.700
so we’ve begun calling them Gates
for the time being.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.320
Gates?

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.250
Some other place?

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.690
Pretty curious...

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:41.130
We’ve hooked us one of
those mega-popular Pikachu!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.220
Following the brat boys all the way
to Sinnoh actually worked!

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.430
Team Rocket!

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.830
Well then, smell nya later!

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.100
You’re not getting away!

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.380
Lucario, I choose you!

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.100
Aura Sphere!

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:05.910
Pikachu!

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.950
Inteleon, go!

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.690
Snipe Shot!

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.880
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.070
Those guys never learn...

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.640
Wh-What?!

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:33.810
That’s a Gate!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.820
Prepare for combat.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.640
Team Rocket, again?

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:44.920
When did they get the time?!

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.960
They sure are persistent...

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.570
Target acquired.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.370
Commence attack.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.200
Evil Pulse!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.460
Inteleon!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.460
Lucario!

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:57.680
Capture them.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.040
Operation complete.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:05.920
Retreat.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:12.090
Stop!

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:15.470
Satoshi?!

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:17.830
Hurry!

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.270
Satoshi!

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.460
Lucario!

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.350
Owww...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.540
Are you okay?

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:34.870
Yeah... Where’s Team Rocket?

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:37.470
We lost them...

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:40.960
Satoshi and Koharu aren’t here,
and the Gate’s gone too...

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.320
Inteleon...!

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.670
That second Team Rocket...

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.080
There was something
different about them.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.220
Yeah.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:56.610
Ms. Junsa said the Gates
could be connected to some other place...

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.980
But it looks exactly the same...

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.780
Something’s strange though...

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:01.740
Yeah...

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.370
Is that...?!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.330
An aurora?!

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.300
No, no, no way...

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.990
You can’t see auroras here, yeah?!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.950
Does that mean...
this really is some other place?

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.260
Hmm...

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:21.340
I know!

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:24.380
If we go to my house,
we might figure something out!

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.340
Something?

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.840
You’ll see when we get there!

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.820
She’s kinda like Satoshi.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.480
This is my house.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:38.720
Well?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.620
Right... Nothing seems different,
as far as I can tell...

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.490
What is it?

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:50.190
When I looked this morning,
the garden was full of blooming flowers.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.810
Flowers, huh...?

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:59.860
Now you mention it, I feel like the park’s flowers vanished
when we went through the Gate, too...

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:02.410
You’re right.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:05.250
But wait...
That might not be all that changed.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.170
The Pokémon!

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.870
Right! They vanished when
we went through the Gate.

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:20.140
I didn’t see any
on the way here, either.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.890
<i>That’s</i> why this all felt so strange!

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.520
Something might’ve happened
to the Pokémon.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:32.030
Sinnoh League, 2nd Place...

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:36.550
This really isn’t my room...

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.100
Which means that this Hikari...

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:41.730
Yeah. She’s a different person.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:42.580
But...

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.080
We both had the same partner...

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.870
Pochama.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:54.460
If there’s another Hikari,
then rather than this being some other place...

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:01.150
Someone’s coming!

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.420
What do we do?

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:05.980
Well, for starters...
I think our best bet’s to hear them out.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:25.470
...then rather than this
being some other place...

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.210
Someone’s coming!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.450
What do we do?

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:37.130
Well, for starters...
I think our best bet’s to hear them out.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.220
She really does look just like you!

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:56.210
Pochama! Oh, what a relief...

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.960
I see... You came through the Gate
and into this world...

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.290
This world?

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:16.060
Those Gates are doors that
connect this world with another one.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:22.520
In other words, you and I are the same person,
living in different worlds.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.330
First, please, let me apologize.

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:32.230
I’m very sorry for taking away
your Pochama.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:36.790
At that moment, I wanted to
return him to you right away,

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.120
but I couldn’t.
The Gate had already closed.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.740
I saw your photos.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.330
You’re close friends with
your Pochama, right?

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.580
Then, I think you can understand...

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.460
How painful it is to have
your Pokémon taken from you.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:03.220
Also, uh, why does nobody
have Pokémon here?

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.100
We didn’t see a single one
on the way here.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.710
Would you come and
meet my Pochama?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.900
Here he is.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:23.470
An egg?!

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:29.240
My Pochama turned back into an egg.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.380
So did all the Pokémon here.

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.450
How...?

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:40.980
One day, strange, shining Gates
began to open all over Sinnoh.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:44.670
Before long,
strange things began to happen.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.400
Pokémon started forgetting
the moves they had learned.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.340
And, almost like time was
moving backwards,

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:56.260
they went back to their
pre-evolved states.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:00.980
Then, finally, even my Pochama...

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:07.080
The affected eggs and Pokémon
are gathered here at this Pokémon Center,

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.230
and Professor Nanakamado is
trying to discover the cause.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:17.480
Then one day, a Gate happened to open,
and showed me a Pochama...

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.560
Excuse me!
That Pochama is my...

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:34.150
It looked so much like
my own Pochama.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.790
I just couldn’t help myself...

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.630
I am sorry.

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:44.410
Don’t worry!
I should apologize, too. I had no idea...

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:49.660
No, I’ve done something
truly unforgivable.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:56.900
Now, your Pokémon will forget their moves too,
and then, in the end...

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:02.570
I don’t want that to happen!
Never!

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:05.320
Go! Can’t we do something?!

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.650
Judging by what we’ve heard so far,

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:12.390
it sounds like space and time
are all messed up...

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:14.600
Space and time...

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.770
...are distorted, you mean?

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:17.880
Yeah.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.900
I think there were some Pokémon
that had to do with those concepts...

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.540
Dialga and Palkia!

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.180
Meanwhile,
as for Satoshi and Koharu...

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:50.130
I wonder if Go, Hikari, and Lucario
are on the other side of that Gate...

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:55.900
Maybe, just maybe,
it could be an entrance to another world.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.400
Another world?!

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:00.260
It was in this novel I read recently.

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:08.600
There was another world just like ours,
and the two were connected by mysterious doors.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:13.200
So if we go to that other world,
we can get Lucario back?!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.370
Y-Yeah...

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.080
And Go and Hikari went there too?!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.460
P-Probably...?

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:22.460
Hey, is there a Pokémon with the power
to go to other worlds?

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:26.300
Hmm... Was there one...?

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:26.840
Oh!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.680
How about Palkia?!

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:30.820
Palkia...

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:33.260
Hey, Rotom.
Can you tell me more about it?

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:38.450
Palkia. Space Pokémon.
Water/Dragon type.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:41.300
It is said to live in a gap
between parallel dimensions.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.490
Its total control
over the boundaries of space...

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:47.820
...enable it to transport itself
to faraway places or even other dimensions.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:53.120
I knew it! If we get Palkia to help us,
we might get to that other world!

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:54.220
Yeah.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:55.830
Any other details?

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.090
Further materials are available
at the Mio Library.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:03.020
The Mio Library...
Let’s check it out!

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:03.880
Yeah!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.800
Koharu! Any luck?

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.900
No... I can’t find anything!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.130
Oh! Ms. Shirona!

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:22.520
Satoshi. What a coincidence.
You’re here alone?

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:23.970
Oh, no...

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:27.280
Oh, I’ll introduce you.
This is my friend.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.400
Nice to meet you. I’m Koharu.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.170
Ms. Shirona is
the Champion of Sinnoh,

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:35.140
and she’s also a scholar researching
Pokémon ruins and stuff.

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:37.200
Huh, that’s amazing!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.660
Thank you.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.540
So, what brings you to this library?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.920
We’re here to read about Palkia.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:49.550
Oh, are you investigating
the recent Pokémon incidents?

00:17:54.310 --> 00:17:58.310
Sinnoh is home to
many myths about Pokémon.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.190
The Legendary Pokémon
ruling over space, Palkia.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:06.510
The Legendary Pokémon
ruling over time, Dialga.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.990
And the one said to have
birthed them both,

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:14.050
the Pokémon said to be a god,
Arceus.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:20.490
Ms. Shirona, what do you think
about the recent incidents?

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:21.920
Hmmm...

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:28.300
Distortions in space could be caused
by Palkia’s tremendous power.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.390
So it <i>is</i> Palkia...

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:33.300
You can stop the
dreary detective act!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.590
Team Rocket!

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:39.810
Those are the thieves!
They stole Satoshi and Go’s Pokémon!

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.220
Give Lucario back!

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:44.510
Stand by for combat.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.900
Let’s go, Gaburias!

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:52.900
Target acquired.

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.610
Commence attack.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.780
Slash!

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.910
Gaburias! Dragon Claw!

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:07.080
Reversed Scale!

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.530
Capture them!

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:13.730
I won’t let you!

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:15.590
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:19.720
Pikachu, what’s wrong?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:25.230
So, the effect has finally reached
this world as well.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.310
Jararanga!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:31.820
Pikachu!

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.140
Reversed Scale!

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:41.780
Withdraw.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.370
Wait!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.800
Satoshi!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.290
Eevee!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.750
Stop, both of you!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.680
You saw that, right?

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.000
I saw the whole thing...

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.900
Those were some
creepy guys, meow.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.370
What was that weird hole
they went through?

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.710
Speak of the devil, here it is...

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.340
Where’s Team Rocket?

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:16.230
They’re gone...
Ms. Shirona, too.

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:17.740
Ahh!

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:19.580
Sorry, Satoshi...

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:24.610
So, is this really another world
that looks just like ours?

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:27.420
Looks like nothing’s changed, to me.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:30.380
Yeah... But something’s strange...

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:35.760
There’s no flowers!

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:36.450
Huh?

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.010
You’re right!

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.400
There’s no Pokémon, either!

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.510
And look!

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:51.960
We might not be able to get
back to our world without that Gate...

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.360
What should we do?

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.770
It’ll work out somehow!

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.900
Let’s start by looking for Go and Hikari!

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.190
Let’s go, Pikachu!

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.370
He’s such a positive thinker...

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.990
Hey! Excuse me!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.170
Me?!

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.070
It’s me?

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.320
Satoshi and Koharu have arrived
in the other world.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:28.730
Meanwhile, Go and the two Hikaris
are researching the distortions in space and time.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:34.110
Will Satoshi and Go be able to
get their Pokémon back?

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:35.480
To be continued!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.600
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.310 --> 00:23:13.200
I’m Satoshi!
What’s your name?

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:16.330
I... I’m Satoshi,
from Masara Town...

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:20.380
It’s not just plants and Pokémon
being rewound.

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:22.110
We humans are being rewound, too!

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:24.720
We heard that Palkia might be
making space distort.

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:28.680
If time is also distorting,
then Dialga might be involved, too!

00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:30.310
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:33.950
Dialga & Palkia!
The Great Space-Time Clash!!
